{
  "id": "feature-detector",
  "term": "feature detector",
  "definition": "A feature detector is a part of an automated analysis method that identifies measurable characteristics in recorded signals, such as peak size, timing-related values, or area under a trace. In this context, it is used to capture features that help distinguish uniform from alternating patterns in calcium current recordings.",
